{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116123","id":3266193677,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7CrikN","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116123","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116123.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116123.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116123","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116123/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116123/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116123/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/f3bd9c2bff3eccd34da7b145c26df3933a9c0f47","number":116123,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add errors for meta types and custom iterators in for loop","user":{"login":"Scrawach","id":40476180,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNDc2MTgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40476180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach","html_url":"https://github.com/Scrawach","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Fixes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116089\r\n\r\n## Example\r\n\r\n<img width=\"957\" height=\"581\" alt=\"example\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a5fd693d-2ed0-4394-93ea-daf2e0717c74\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>GDScript source code</summary>\r\n\r\n``` gdscript\r\nfunc _ready() -> void:\r\n\tfor i in Object:\t\t\t\t\t# native meta type\r\n\t\tpass\r\n\tfor i in BadIterator.new():\t\t\t# user type without `_iter` methods\r\n\t\tpass\r\n\tfor i in Iterator:\t\t\t\t\t# user meta type\r\n\t\tpass\r\n\tfor i in Iterator.new():\t\t\t# user type with all `_iter` methods\r\n\t\tpass\r\n\tfor i in PartIterator.new():\t\t# user type with only 1 `_iter` method (required 3)\r\n\t\tpass\r\n\tfor i in ChildIterator.new():\t\t# user type extends `Iterator`\r\n\t\tpass\r\n\tfor i in Object.new():\t\t\t\t# nativa type without `_iter` methods overriden\r\n\t\tpass\r\n\tfor i in PackedDataContainer.new():\t# native type with `_iter` methods overriden\r\n\t\tpass\r\n\tfor i in CustomDataContainer.new():\t# user type extends `PackedDataContainer`\r\n\t\tpass\r\n\r\nclass BadIterator:\r\n\tfunc do() -> void:\r\n\t\tpass\r\n\r\nclass PartIterator:\r\n\tfunc _iter_get(iter: Variant) -> Variant:\r\n\t\treturn null\r\n\r\nclass Iterator:\r\n\tfunc _iter_get(iter: Variant) -> Variant:\r\n\t\treturn null\r\n\tfunc _iter_init(iter: Array) -> bool:\r\n\t\treturn true\r\n\tfunc _iter_next(iter: Array) -> bool:\r\n\t\treturn false\r\n\r\nclass ChildIterator extends Iterator:\r\n\tfunc _iter_init(iter: Array) -> bool:\r\n\t\tprint(iter)\r\n\t\treturn super._iter_init(iter)\r\n\r\nclass CustomDataContainer extends PackedDataContainer:\r\n\tvar title: String\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\nTo detect overridden `_iter()` methods in native types, I check `METHOD_FLAG_OBJECT_CORE` flag. It looks a bit hacky, but it works and shouldn't break in future.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","co